{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Status: change MERGED, ticket held open by a verifier infrastructure loop\n\nGerrit change 1434 is **MERGED** on `main` (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved\ncomments). All acceptance criteria are met and ticked.\n\nThe close is blocked on the completion-verification gate, which failed twice — at the default\nstep budget and again at `REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS=1200`. Its own telemetry shows a non-progressing\nloop, not an under-sized budget: `max_consecutive_repeat=131` on a single identical\n`search_files` signature out of 260 total tool calls. Raising the budget only lets it loop\nlonger, which is why the second attempt failed identically.\n\n`--force-close` was deliberately NOT used: it discards the completion attestation, and an\ninfrastructure loop is not a reason to drop a safety gate. Filed as bug\n46a2-9c1a-d855-4706 (`brusque-tippable-sunbittern`), linked `discovered_from` this ticket.\n\nThis ticket stays `in_progress` until that verifier bug is fixed or an operator decides to\nforce-close it. The work itself is complete and landed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785954361288449001,"uuid":"81b046dc-b0fe-49ab-9152-6e74c63c63d9"}